            <ArticleTitle>Nonalcoholic fatty liver disease and the PNPLA3 gene.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>101-6, 121</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nonalcoholic fatty liver disease, a potentially fatal obesity-related condition, affects more than 70 million people in the United States. Nurses are well-positioned to impact this genetically influenced disease by is increasing awareness, providing patient education, and advocating for affected persons.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
